<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amynander</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 200–189 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Amynander of Athamania</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amynander was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athamanians">Athamanians</a> in the mountains of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> around the end of the 3rd and start of the 2nd century BCE. He joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-macedon">Philip V of Macedon</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-macedonian-war">Second Macedonian War</a> and acted as an intermediary, then sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> in 191 BCE, when Philip overran his kingdom and he fled to Ambracia. He later regained his throne and made peace with Rome.</p></div>
